id: SECRETS-042
title: Redis URI with Password
category: secrets
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .ts .tsx .js .jsx .py .java .go .rb .rs .cpp .h .cs .php .env .yml .yaml .json .toml .xml .properties .cfg .ini .conf .sh .tf .hcl
  exclude_paths: test/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/ __pycache__/ .venv/ target/
patterns:
  - regex: redis://:[^@]+@
    message: Redis connection string with embedded password detected. Redis credentials in URIs are exposed in logs.
  - regex: redis://[^:]+:[^@]+@
    message: Redis connection string with embedded credentials detected. Credentials in URIs are exposed in logs.
fix: Use environment variables (e.g., REDIS_URL) loaded at runtime from a secrets manager. Configure Redis ACLs for fine-grained access.
